const title = "Frigidaire Dishwasher Not Draining: i20/i40 — Same Day";
const description = "Frigidaire dishwasher won't drain, or showing i20 or i40? The fix is the glass trap/filter, drain hose, disposal plug, or air gap. Many models show no code at all. $89.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why is my Frigidaire dishwasher not draining?",
    a: "On a Frigidaire the standing water almost always traces to a clogged glass trap or filter, a kinked or clogged drain hose, a disposal knockout plug left in after a new disposal, a blocked sink air gap, or a failed drain pump. The first four are homeowner-checkable; the pump is the tech job. Frigidaire's drain codes are i20 (\"did not drain properly\") and i40 (\"clogged filter or sump\"), but many Frigidaire models show no code at all — they just leave water in the tub. Either way the fix path is the same, and it starts with the glass trap and filter. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What do the i20 and i40 codes mean on a Frigidaire dishwasher?",
    a: "Per Frigidaire's own support site, i20 means the dishwasher did not drain properly — a blockage in the filter, sump, drain hose, disposal, or air gap, or a weak drain pump. i40 means a clogged filter or sump from food-soil buildup, and Frigidaire's fix is to clean the glass trap and filter. Both are drain codes and share the same cleanup steps. Note that i30 is a different code — it's a leak/flood warning (water in the base pan), not a drain error — so don't treat an i30 as a drain clog."
  },
  {
    q: "My Frigidaire dishwasher won't drain but shows no error code — is that normal?",
    a: "Yes. Many Frigidaire dishwashers, especially basic and older models with an LED-bar or no alphanumeric display, don't show a drain code at all. They simply won't drain and leave standing water. Frigidaire's own \"not draining\" guidance routes those owners straight to the same checks — glass trap and filter, drain hose, disposal knockout plug, and air gap — with no code involved. So a missing code doesn't mean a mystery; work the same list."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I clean the filter or glass trap on a Frigidaire dishwasher?",
    a: "It depends on your model, so check yours first. Some Frigidaire dishwashers have a removable filter you twist out and rinse; others have a self-managing glass trap that Frigidaire says to clean in place — wipe out visible food and glass from the trap area but do not disassemble it. Do not force a filter that isn't designed to come out. If you're unsure which type you have, clean what's visible in the sump, run a rinse cycle, and if it still won't drain, we'll sort the right filter service on a visit. Watch for broken glass in the trap."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I clear a Frigidaire dishwasher that won't drain?",
    a: "Safe, in order: scoop out the standing water, clean the glass trap and filter area (remove visible food and glass; only twist out the filter if your model has a removable one), check the drain hose behind the unit for a kink or clog and confirm the required high loop, run the garbage disposal (a full one blocks the shared drain, and a new disposal may still have its knockout plug), and clear the sink air gap. Use only dishwasher detergent. Re-run a rinse cycle. If water still stands, it's the drain pump — that's our job."
  }
];

